### ============================================================
### Health & OpenAPI — events-bff (port 8080)
###
### `bff-host` already carries the base path, so no request here
### spells one. It is empty locally and `/api` on a cluster,
### because Spring serves the prefix there and not locally.
### ============================================================

### Health check (Actuator) — LOCAL ONLY
###
### The chart moves the actuator to MANAGEMENT_SERVER_PORT=9001, which no
### ingress rule names, so this cannot answer on a cluster by design. Against
### `staging` it returns 404 from the BFF, which is the honest answer — before
### `bff-host` carried `/api` the same request fell through to the frontend's
### SPA fallback and returned 200, which read as a healthy actuator.
GET {{bff-host}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI spec (JSON)
GET {{bff-host}}/v3/api-docs
Accept: application/json

### Swagger UI (open in browser)
GET {{bff-host}}/webjars/swagger-ui/index.html

### Hello endpoint (internal smoke test)
GET {{bff-host}}/hello
Accept: text/plain
